reconstructed_theorem_text:
For every type E equipped with a normed additive commutative group structure, a real inner-product-space structure, finite-dimensionality over R, a measurable-space structure and a compatible BorelSpace structure (including dimension zero), every V : E -> R, alpha,beta : R_{>=0}, and eta : R, assume:
(1) 0 < (alpha : R);
(2) alpha <= beta;
(3) V is ContDiff R 2;
(4) for every x,v in E,
    (alpha : R)*||v||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x v) v
    and (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x v) v <= (beta : R)*||v||^2;
(5) 0 < eta;
(6) (beta : R)*eta <= 1.
Define, using the exact normalized exponential tilt and canonical volume,
mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (x |-> -V(x));
J := (mu.prod (stdGaussian E)).map ((x,z) |-> (x, x + sqrt(eta) * z));
nu := J.snd;
S(y) := (volume : Measure E).tilted
        (u |-> -V((1/2) * (y+u)) - ||y-u||^2/(8*eta)).
Here scalar multiplication is the real scalar action on E and stdGaussian E is the standard Gaussian law.
Then nu is a probability measure, and there exists a single real-linear partial map
G : Lp R 2 nu ->_partial Lp E 2 nu
such that its linear-subspace domain is dense in the entire Lp R 2 nu space, G is closable, and the graph of its genuine closure is closed. Its graph has exactly the following characterization: for every u in Lp R 2 nu and v in Lp E 2 nu,
(u,v) belongs to G.graph if and only if there exists phi : E -> R that is ContDiff R infinity and has compact support, with u equal to phi nu-almost everywhere and v equal to gradient(phi) nu-almost everywhere.
For that same G, for every f : E -> R that is ContDiff R infinity and has compact support, let
Tf(y) := integral [u in E] f(u) dS(y)(u).
There exist hTf : MemLp Tf 2 nu and hGrad : MemLp (gradient Tf) 2 nu such that
(hTf.toLp Tf, hGrad.toLp (gradient Tf)) belongs to G.closure.graph.
The integral is the actual real Bochner integral, the gradient is the genuine real Hilbert Frechet gradient, and the two toLp terms are the canonical almost-everywhere L2 classes of these literal functions.
